{
  // WHY A SECOND tsconfig: the root `tsconfig.json` has `"include": ["src/**/*"]` with
  // `"rootDir": "src"`, so `vitest.config.ts` is outside the program entirely — and
  // `eslint.config.mjs` uses the non-type-aware recommended set, so ESLint does not read it
  // either. A config key that STOPS EXISTING therefore stops doing anything without
  // stopping compiling. That is not hypothetical: `poolOptions` (removed in Vitest 4) and a
  // per-project `teardownTimeout` (root-only) both sat in `vitest.config.ts` doing nothing,
  // under comments describing what they were supposed to do, and were found by measurement
  // months later (#655). Under the Vitest 4 types both were already compile errors.
  //
  // It cannot be folded into the root tsconfig: `rootDir: "src"` forbids inputs outside
  // `src/`, and widening it would move every emitted path in `dist/`.
  //
  // Run by `npm run check:config-types`, next to the other `check:*` gates.
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "ES2022",
    "module": "NodeNext",
    "moduleResolution": "NodeNext",
    "strict": true,
    "esModuleInterop": true,
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "noEmit": true
  },
  // Every root-level file spelled `*.config.{ts,mts,cts}`. Today that is `vitest.config.ts`
  // alone, and a NEW one spelled that way is covered without touching this file.
  //
  // THE PROMISE IS ABOUT EXTENSIONS, NOT BASENAMES (gate 2, 2026-09-15). A root TypeScript
  // config that does not spell `.config.` — `vitest.workspace.ts`, a `knip.ts` — is NOT matched
  // and has to be added here by hand. Widening to `*.ts` would instead pull in whatever else
  // ever lands at the root, so the pattern stays narrow and the gap is stated.
  //
  // ALL THREE EXTENSIONS, and that is the point: a glob of `*.config.ts` alone leaves a
  // `*.config.mts` or `*.config.cts` silently uncovered — this PR's own defect, one file
  // extension over (gate 2, win2, 2026-09-15). The set of TypeScript config extensions is
  // closed and is these three; a JS config (`eslint.config.mjs`) is out of reach without
  // `allowJs`/`checkJs`, which is a bigger decision than this file.
  //
  // If every matching file ever disappeared, `tsc` fails with "No inputs were found" — loud,
  // not silent (measured in the same round).
  "include": ["*.config.ts", "*.config.mts", "*.config.cts"],
  "exclude": ["node_modules", "dist"]
}
